From 33cbe3d23ce0900dec2229a5b9cf9520a17c2a66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guilherme Silva <239806034+NoneSilva@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:31:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bind the MCP server to loopback

The MCP server listened on 0.0.0.0, so the network could reach it, and
it has no authentication. The new setting elixirLS.mcpHost chooses the
host it listens on. The default is localhost, so it stays on loopback.
The bridge script takes the host as an optional second argument.

A failure to listen no longer stops the language server, and the
accept loop stops when the listen socket closes.
